{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Because you have done this.</b> From here we learn that one does not plead merit on behalf of an inciter — for had they asked him, 'Why did you do this?', he could have answered: 'The words of the master and the words of the student — whose words are heard?' (Sanhedrin 29)." "<b>From all the cattle and from all the beast of the field.</b> If it was cursed more than cattle, then more than wild beast all the more so. Our Sages set this midrash in tractate Bekhorot (8a) to teach that the gestation period of the serpent is seven years." "<b>On your belly you shall go.</b> It had legs, and they were cut off."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:24.355405921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}